ons and storage, available to the general public over the internet. Resources may be free, or sold on a pay-per-usage model. On the other hand, a **Private Cloud** is a type of cloud computing that delivers similar advantages to public cloud, including scalability and self-service, but through a proprietary architecture dedicated to a single organization. Unlike public clouds, which deliver services to multiple organizations, a private cloud is dedicated to the needs and goals of a single entity. Lastly, a **Hybrid Cloud** is a solution that combines a private cloud with one or more public cloud services, with proprietary software enabling communication between each distinct service.","title":"Bare Metal vs VMs vs Containers","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Types of Cloud Computing","url":"https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/cloud-computing/public-cloud-vs-private-cloud-and-hybrid-cloud","_id":"68a7360cf1191f340e113ac5"},{"type":"article","title":"Selecting the right cloud for workloads","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/public-sector-cloud-transformation/selecting-the-right-cloud-for-workloads-differences-between-public-private-and-hybrid.html","_id":"68a7360cf1191f340e113ac6"}],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"Py9nst2FDJ1_hoXeX_qSF","title":"Introduction"}],"description":"# Public vs Private vs Hybrid Cloud\n\nAmazon Web Services (AWS) offers various cloud-based deployment models to cater to varying business needs, including Public, Private, and Hybrid clouds. A **Public Cloud** is a model where the service provider offers resources, such as applications and storage, a...","order":46,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"43drPbTwPqJQPyzwYUdBT","fullDescription":"","title":"Docker and OCI","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"Py9nst2FDJ1_hoXeX_qSF","title":"Introduction"}],"description":"","order":47,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"NCdsPRhJy7UtQFNLo1J1f","fullDescription":"","title":"Docker Desktop (Win/Mac/Linux)","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"01nDXqxVdMv4SeXc0nYHH","title":"Installation / Setup"}],"description":"","order":48,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"0NKqLUWtJMlXn-m6wpA6f","fullDescription":"","title":"Docker Engine ( Linux )","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"01nDXqxVdMv4SeXc0nYHH","title":"Installation / Setup"}],"description":"","order":49,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"01nDXqxVdMv4SeXc0nYHH","fullDescription":"","title":"Installation / Setup","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"jrH1qE6EnFXL4fTyYU8gR","title":"Underlying Technologies"}],"description":"","order":50,"leadsTo":[{"nodeId":"NCdsPRhJy7UtQFNLo1J1f","title":"Docker Desktop (Win/Mac/Linux)"},{"nodeId":"0NKqLUWtJMlXn-m6wpA6f","title":"Docker Engine ( Linux )"}]},{"nodeId":"Py9nst2FDJ1_hoXeX_qSF","fullDescription":"# Introduction\n\nAWS (Amazon Web Services) offers a broad set of global cloud-based products including compute, storage, databases, analytics, networking, mobile, developer tools, management tools, IoT, security, and enterprise applications: on-demand, available in seconds, with pay-as-you-go pricing. From data warehousing to deployment tools, directories to content delivery, over 200 AWS services are available. New services can be provisioned quickly, without the upfront fixed expense. This allows enterprises, start-ups, small and medium-sized businesses, and customers in the public sector to access the building blocks they need to respond quickly to changing business requirements. This whitepaper provides you with an overview of the benefits of the AWS Cloud and introduces you to the services that make up the platform.","title":"Introduction","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"AWS Documentation","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/","_id":"68a7360cf1191f340e113aae"},{"type":"official","title":"Introduction of AWS","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/aws-overview/introduction.html","_id":"68a7360cf1191f340e113aaf"},{"type":"article","title":"How to Create an AWS Account","url":"https://grapplingdev.com/tutorials/how-to-create-aws-account","_id":"68a7360cf1191f340e113ab0"},{"type":"video","title":"AWS Tutorial for Beginners","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zA8guDqfv40","_id":"68a7360cf1191f340e113ab1"}],"prerequisites":[],"description":"# Introduction\n\nAWS (Amazon Web Services) offers a broad set of global cloud-based products including compute, storage, databases, analytics, networking, mobile, developer tools, management tools, IoT, security, and enterprise applications: on-demand, available in seconds, with pay-as-you-go pricing...","order":51,"leadsTo":[{"nodeId":"74JxgfJ_1qmVNZ_QRp9Ne","title":"What are Containers?"},{"nodeId":"i4ijY3T5gLgNz0XqRipXe","title":"Why do we need Containers?"},{"nodeId":"3hatcMVLDbMuz73uTx-9P","title":"Bare Metal vs VMs vs Containers"},{"nodeId":"43drPbTwPqJQPyzwYUdBT","title":"Docker and OCI"},{"nodeId":"jrH1qE6EnFXL4fTyYU8gR","title":"Underlying Technologies"}]},{"nodeId":"BvV8VCX39wRB-g8WvGF1g","fullDescription":"","title":"Namespaces","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"jrH1qE6EnFXL4fTyYU8gR","title":"Underlying Technologies"}],"description":"","order":52,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"jrH1qE6EnFXL4fTyYU8gR","fullDescription":"","title":"Underlying Technologies","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"Py9nst2FDJ1_hoXeX_qSF","title":"Introduction"}],"description":"","order":53,"leadsTo":[{"nodeId":"vEUfw_vobshuZI0-q8RZo","title":"Union Filesystems"},{"nodeId":"BvV8VCX39wRB-g8WvGF1g","title":"Namespaces"},{"nodeId":"01nDXqxVdMv4SeXc0nYHH","title":"Installation / Setup"}]},{"nodeId":"vEUfw_vobshuZI0-q8RZo","fullDescription":"","title":"Union Filesystems","resources":[],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"jrH1qE6EnFXL4fTyYU8gR","title":"Underlying Technologies"}],"description":"","order":54,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"74JxgfJ_1qmVNZ_QRp9Ne","fullDescription":"# What is Cloud Computing?\n\nCloud Computing refers to the delivery of computing services over the internet instead of using local servers. It offers reliable, scalable, and inexpensive cloud computing services which include data storage, databases, applications, analytics, machine learning, and even setting up virtual servers. The biggest names providing cloud computing services are Amazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud, and others. The main selling point is that you only pay for the services you use, helping you manage your expenses more effectively.","title":"What are Containers?","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What is Cloud Computing - IBM","url":"https://www.ibm.com/topics/cloud-computing","_id":"68a7360cf1191f340e113ae6"},{"type":"article","title":"Cloud Computing - AWS","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/what-is-cloud-computing/","_id":"68a7360cf1191f340e113ae7"}],"prerequisites":[{"nodeId":"Py9nst2FDJ1_hoXeX_qSF","title":"Introduction"}],"description":"# What is Cloud Computing?\n\nCloud Computing refers to the delivery of computing services over the internet instead of using local servers. It offers reliable, scalable, and inexpensive cloud computing services which include data storage, databases, applications, analytics, machine learning, and even...","order":55,"leadsTo":[]},{"nodeId":"i4ijY3T5gLgNz0XqRipXe","fullDescription":"# IaaS vs PaaS vs SaaS\n\nIaaS, PaaS, and SaaS are three types of cloud service models. **IaaS** or Infrastructure as a Service provides users with a resource-based service via virtualization technology, offering computing infrastructure, physical or (more often) virtual machines and other resources. **PaaS** or Platform as a Service provides runtime environments for developing, testing, and managing applications, it is utilized for software development and offers a platform to developers to build applications and services over the internet. **SaaS** or Software as a Service provides on-demand software accessed via the internet, it delivers a complete software solution that you purchase on a pay-as-you-go basis from a cloud service provider.","title":"Why do we need Containers?"